From 273bf87a108cbcc4745e0fececd47ac706659c7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:13:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a translated system turn is folded for a Responses
 upstream, and a relay's "Upstream request failed" 400 fails a group over
 (#4632)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two faults, one turn. Claude Code 2.1.296 and later send their
environment as a message with role "system" inside messages
(Request.envInTurns). The Chat and Anthropic builds fold such a message
into the system prompt (responseInstructions); buildResponses wrote the
role as it came, and a relay whose Responses endpoint fronts the ChatGPT
backend — which takes user, assistant and developer alone — answered
every translated turn 400 "Upstream request failed". That 400 matched
none of the wordings that make a 4xx retryable, so the holdWriter held
it as final and the group's second member never ran: the relay's answer
went to the agent, every turn.

What changed: buildResponses folds a translated request's system and
developer messages the way the Chat and Anthropic builds do, keyed on
the read. A Responses client's own instruction items are kept by the
read (#2532) and go where they stood; so do a codex account's, which
its send says as developer ones in place (codexBody — the fold would
move them out of conversation order, so buildFor marks the account's
requests kept). A translated request's system message is the harness's,
so it is said in the instructions, and one after a reply is told as a
user <system-reminder>, as on every other target. A relay's own word
that the provider behind it turned the request away ("sub2api: Upstream
request failed", type upstream_error — the words the Codex compaction
already reads, #866, #1511) joins the wordings that make a 400 or 422
retryable (retryable) and fail a group over (shapeRefused): the next
member is asked, and nobody rests. A 400 that says nothing of the kind
still ends the route, as a bad request would fail on every member
alike.

Run: TestClaudeSystemTurnSaidInTheInstructionsOnResponses and
TestGroupFailsOverARelaysUpstreamFailed, red at upstream/main 77e853588
and green here; TestUpstreamFailedWordsFailARelayOver's guards (a 401,
403 or 429 with the words, a plain bad request, and an
insufficient_quota beside them keep their reading); the codex account's
own shape (TestCodexAccountUpstream, both clients), the instruction
roles contract (TestResponsesInstructionRolesThroughSearch,
TestResponsesInstructionsOtherAPIsUnchanged), the compaction, group and
retry families, the full gateway package, gofmt, vet on darwin, linux
and windows, and builds of all three (-tags nogui).

